  <component>
    <structuredBody>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34066-1" displayName="BOXED WARNING SECTION"/>
          <title>WARNING: PREMATURE DISCONTINUATION INCREASES THE RISK OF THROMBOTIC EVENTS</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>Premature discontinuation of ELIQUIS increases the risk of thrombotic events.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>Do not discontinue ELIQUIS without considering alternative anticoagulation.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34067-9" displayName="INDICATIONS &amp; USAGE SECTION"/>
          <title>1 INDICATIONS AND USAGE</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>ELIQUIS is indicated to reduce the risk of stroke and systemic embolism.</paragraph>
          </text>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="42229-5"/>
              <title>1.1 Adult patients</title>
              <text><paragraph>The source hierarchy remains explicit.</paragraph></text>
            </section>
          </component>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34068-7" displayName="DOSAGE &amp; ADMINISTRATION SECTION"/>
          <title>2 DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>The recommended dose is 5 mg taken orally twice daily.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>Use 2.5 mg twice daily when at least two characteristics are present: age ≥ 80 years, body weight ≤ 60 kg, or serum creatinine ≥ 1.5 mg/dL.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>Do not double the dose to make up for a missed dose.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="43678-2" displayName="DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS SECTION"/>
          <title>3 DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS</title>
          <text><paragraph>Tablets: 2.5 mg and 5 mg.</paragraph></text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34070-3" displayName="CONTRAINDICATIONS SECTION"/>
          <title>4 CONTRAINDICATIONS</title>
          <text>
            <list>
              <item>Active pathological bleeding.</item>
              <item>Severe hypersensitivity reaction to apixaban.</item>
            </list>
          </text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="43685-7" displayName="WARNINGS AND PRECAUTIONS SECTION"/>
          <title>5 WARNINGS AND PRECAUTIONS</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>ELIQUIS increases the risk of bleeding and can cause serious, potentially fatal bleeding.</paragraph>
            <paragraph>Concomitant medicines affecting hemostasis may increase this risk; use is not recommended when evidence is insufficient.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34084-4" displayName="ADVERSE REACTIONS SECTION"/>
          <title>6 ADVERSE REACTIONS</title>
          <text><paragraph>The most common adverse reactions involve bleeding.</paragraph></text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34073-7" displayName="DRUG INTERACTIONS SECTION"/>
          <title>7 DRUG INTERACTIONS</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>Combined P-gp and strong CYP3A4 inhibitors increase blood levels of apixaban.</paragraph>
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Concomitant drug</th><th>Source-label instruction</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Strong dual inhibitors</td><td>Reduce the dose by 50% in specified patients.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Rifampin</td><td>Avoid concomitant use.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="43684-0" displayName="USE IN SPECIFIC POPULATIONS SECTION"/>
          <title>8 USE IN SPECIFIC POPULATIONS</title>
          <text><paragraph>Population-specific source subsections follow.</paragraph></text>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="42228-7" displayName="PREGNANCY SECTION"/>
              <title>8.1 Pregnancy</title>
              <text><paragraph>Available data are insufficient to inform a drug-associated risk.</paragraph></text>
            </section>
          </component>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="77290-5" displayName="LACTATION SECTION"/>
              <title>8.2 Lactation</title>
              <text/>
            </section>
          </component>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="34081-0" displayName="PEDIATRIC USE SECTION"/>
              <title>8.4 Pediatric Use</title>
              <text><paragraph>Use only the source-described pediatric presentation and dose.</paragraph></text>
            </section>
          </component>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="34082-8" displayName="GERIATRIC USE SECTION"/>
              <title>8.5 Geriatric Use</title>
              <text><paragraph>No clinically significant differences were observed in the cited studies.</paragraph></text>
            </section>
          </component>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="42229-5"/>
              <title>8.6 Renal Impairment</title>
              <text><paragraph>Renal-impairment wording is preserved without inference.</paragraph></text>
            </section>
          </component>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="42229-5"/>
              <title>8.7 Hepatic Impairment</title>
              <text><paragraph>Hepatic-impairment wording is preserved without inference.</paragraph></text>
            </section>
          </component>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34088-5" displayName="OVERDOSAGE SECTION"/>
          <title>10 OVERDOSAGE</title>
          <text><paragraph>Overdose increases the risk of bleeding.</paragraph></text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34090-1" displayName="CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY SECTION"/>
          <title>12 CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY</title>
          <text><paragraph>Apixaban is a selective inhibitor of Factor Xa.</paragraph></text>
        </section>
      </component>
      <component>
        <section>
          <code code="34069-5" displayName="HOW SUPPLIED SECTION"/>
          <title>16 HOW SUPPLIED/STORAGE AND HANDLING</title>
          <text><paragraph>ELIQUIS tablets are supplied in labeled containers.</paragraph></text>
          <component>
            <section>
              <code code="44425-7" displayName="STORAGE AND HANDLING SECTION"/>
              <title>Storage and Handling</title>
              <text><paragraph>Store at 20°C to 25°C (68°F to 77°F).</paragraph></text>
            </section>
          </component>
        </section>
      </component>
